{title: Victory Over Death}
{subtitle: 1 Corinthians 15:55–57}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] | [Cm7] |
| [Cm7] | [Abmaj7] | [Abmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]The trumpet sounds in a blink of an [Bb/D]eye
[Cm7]The dead rise up to live eternal[Bb6]ly
This [Abmaj7]perishable puts on what is immortal
[Bb]The mortal body is changed by the call
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Where O death is your [Eb]victory
Where O death is your [Cm]sting
The sting of death is [Abmaj7]sin
But [Bb]God gives us the vic[Eb]tory
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Thanks be to God for the [Bb/D]win
[Cm]Through our Lord Jesus Christ we [Bb]begin
[Abmaj7]Be steadfast and immovable stand
[Bb]Always abounding in the Lord's hand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Where O death is [Eb]your victory
Where O death is your [Cm]sting
The sting of death is [Abmaj7]sin
But [Bb]God gives us the vic[Eb]tory
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]Labor in the Lord is not [Bb]vain
[Eb/G]Hope remains for us in [Cm]the rain
[Ab]The law held power over [Bb]sin
[Ab]But Christ has [Bb]broken the chain
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Death has been swallowed [Cm]up
Victory is ours [Abmaj7]to [Bb][Eb]keep
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] | [Abmaj7] | [Bb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
